  "result_interpretation": "Strict future-day temporal holdout. After Policy A deduplication, the test period contains 50,306 attacks out of 1,631,630 rows (3.08%); the surviving attack families are bot (15,214), infiltration (34,807), and web attacks (285), none of which appear in the earlier training window. Random Forest accuracy is 0.9633, but F1 is 0.0113, recall 0.0068, and ROC-AUC 0.3905. The random-split CSE RF F1 of 0.8861 is an in-domain upper bound: bot recall falls from 0.9917 (random) to 0.00085 (temporal), infiltration from 0.1070 to 0.0094, and web/XSS/SQL to zero. This is a negative future-day generalization result, not a replacement for the in-domain benchmark.",
